+# Inquiry acceptance status - 0.6.1
+
+This is a reset-correction release. It is not acceptance of live repeat-inquiry activation.
+
+## Confirmed cause and correction
+
+The installed FluentCRM 3.2.6 method deletes explicitly supplied blank custom-field keys only when its second argument, deleteOtherValues, is true. Ads Bridge 0.6.0 passed false for both the repeat-inquiry reset and Unqualified's stale qualification clearing. Its merge-only test doubles incorrectly treated those calls as deleting fields.
+
+The corrected test doubles reproduce installed deletion behavior. The inquiry test dispatches the real Ads Bridge lifecycle and inquiry callbacks. On the unpatched source, the corrected lifecycle suite reported 17 PASS / 1 FAIL and the inquiry suite reported 20 PASS / 2 FAIL. The old contact retained previous dates/revenue despite a committed activation response, and the new inquiry could inherit a false Won milestone.
+
+0.6.1 uses selective deletion and suppresses Ads Bridge's timestamp restoration during projection. It verifies the persisted activating marker before resetting, validates reset configuration, re-reads contact fields/tags, and returns retry rather than acknowledging failed projection. Incomplete activations suppress lifecycle stamping and active-history mirroring for that contact. Configured field aliases are also cleared; unrelated fields, CRM Ops identity, consent values and non-lifecycle tags are preserved.
+
+## Scope and evidence
+
+- Three same-site PHP adapters remain adopt / prepare / commit; contract version 1.
+- Inquiry schema remains 1. No extra migration is needed over migrated 0.6.0.
+- All_Leads remains 94 columns; Google_Ads_Import remains 21.
+- Tests are isolated PHP tests with a simulated database and Subscriber. They do not exercise the installed FluentCRM sanitizer, database transactions, database locks, actual mail, or Google/Sheets.
+- Local test PHP is 8.3.6. The deployed 0.6.0 PHP 8.4.27 runtime has passed its aggregate dry-run and scheduled-export doctor check. The 0.6.1 build still needs server PHP 8.4 validation after installation.
+- No adoption, prepare, commit or repeat-inquiry recovery has been run live on the Golden site in this continuation.
+- CRM Ops inquiry runtime remains unimplemented. Its operational fields and email drafts do not implement inquiry identity or reconciliation.
+
+## Remaining work before live repeat activation
+
+1. Enforce head-version comparison at prepare and activation; current version fields are stored but do not provide compare-and-swap protection.
+2. Serialize concurrent contact transitions across requests and coordinate that protection with CRM Ops. The request-local projection guard is not a database lock.
+3. Validate transactional storage and check all inquiry archive/activate and transaction-control results. The contact reset precedes that transaction and is not atomically committed with CRM Ops.
+4. Define durable recovery after partial projection or a process crash. Identical retries can repeat the reset; no recovery worker, projection checkpoint, or compensation adapter exists. Customer activity must remain held during an incomplete activation.
+5. Define stale/replayed-event behavior after later inquiry transitions and test identity conflicts and contention.
+6. Implement CRM Ops inquiry creation, adoption-before-replacement and the prepare / head activation / committed-ack hold. The proposed CRM Ops events do not have Ads Bridge listeners.
+7. Run live tests for old Won -> new inquiry, prior unexported milestones, retry/fault cases, immutable identity/consent binding, DNC suppression, and independent stage ledgers.
+
+Do not enable Start New Inquiry or customer-facing inquiry sends based on the reset test results alone.
